<!--
    kuna-bitscan: abs and the one-instruction bit-scan loops (option bitidioms).

    Source (clang -O2, x86-64):
      int iabs(int x) { return x < 0 ? -x : x; }     neg eax ; cmovs eax,edi
      int ctz(unsigned x) { return __builtin_ctz(x); }  tzcnt eax,edi
      int clz(unsigned x) { return __builtin_clz(x); }  bsr eax,edi ; xor eax,0x1f

    SLEIGH lifts cmovs as a branch around a copy and tzcnt/bsr as loops inside
    the one instruction. Stage: P3 simplification (RuleIntAbs, the MULTIEQUAL
    of x and -x chosen by a sign test) and the returnsplit-group action
    ActionBitScanLoop, which proves the loop by running it on every single-bit
    source and rewrites it to ctz(x) or LZCOUNT(x) ^ 0x1f.

    Pass 1 (default) prints abs(a0), ctz(a0) and LZCOUNT; pass 2 (bitidioms off)
    prints the cmov diamond and the loops.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true">
